  "question": "For the historical requirements relevant to the current client task, reconstruct their last valid state immediately before the current task. Do not apply the current task to that state.",
  "target_task": {
    "source_message_id": 9,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Dom,\n\nBecause this is a sample piece, you have carte blanche and I’ll defer to your judgment. Let me know if there is anything you need from me.\n\nNate"
  },
  "history_pool": {
    "boundary": "STRICTLY_BEFORE_TARGET_MESSAGE",
    "contains_target_message": false,
    "message_count": 8,
    "messages": [
      {
        "message_id": 1,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "freelancer",
        "text": "Nathaniel, thank you for replying so quickly. I’ll address each of your questions below.\n\n1. My initial thought was to begin at the start and adapt as much of the story as possible. If you would rather have me concentrate on a particular section, though, I can do that instead.\n\n2. The sample folder I shared shows my usual script style. For every page, I recommend using a panel format. Although I sometimes indicate caption placement, I generally leave the precise positioning of dialogue balloons and similar elements to the artist.\n\n3. Because I would be adapting your script, I would shape the pacing and structure mainly by choosing how many panels, or how much page space, each moment receives. Those decisions should be reasonably self-explanatory, but I can explain them after writing if you would like. Including explanatory notes would require additional time, which would also raise my rate for the larger project.\n\nI look forward to your response.",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 2,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "While I continue evaluating all candidates next Monday, I’ll hold off on a final choice and make my decision by noon (my time). Thank you for the excellent response, and please send over any questions you may have.",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 3,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "Dom,\n\nI have one last question: how much time would you need to complete this sample project?\n\nThanks!\nNate",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 4,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "freelancer",
        "text": "My target would be to return the script by the following Thursday, provided I can begin next Monday. That schedule would leave a gap between the first and second drafts while also reserving time to address any questions that arise.\n\nThanks,\nDom",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 5,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "The 18-page sample is something I’d like to move forward with. Let me know if you accept, and I’ll send the contract under the terms already discussed in our messages. Please raise any questions you have; otherwise, I’ll send it out shortly. Thanks!",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 6,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "For additional context, I’ve attached several other files. If you need more material or have any questions, just let me know. I’m available throughout the day and, when necessary, at night as well. Thanks!",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 7,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "freelancer",
        "text": "Because the project appears to have already been funded, I’ll get started in the early afternoon. I’ll contact you if any questions arise, and regardless, I’ll try to provide an update by midday next Tuesday.",
        "milestone": null
      },
      {
        "message_id": 8,
        "created_ts": null,
        "speaker": "freelancer",
        "text": "Today’s progress has been good: I’ve drafted a tentative breakdown that reaches Tom’s meeting with Apollonia on comic page 18. As I continue, I may find that this pace is too brisk if some beats require more room to breathe.\n\nBefore proceeding further, I want to check two questions—or, more accurately, two thoughts about the script—with you:\n\n1.. In several places, I may adapt portions of the scene descriptions into \"voice over\" caption text.\n\n2\\. To use the available page space efficiently, I may omit a few brief exchanges. One example is at the bottom of page 41, where Carter tells Tom that he is invited to the dinner shown in the following scene.\n\nWould deviations of this size be acceptable, or should the comic reproduce the screenplay line-for-line? Let me know what you think.\n\nThanks.",
        "milestone": null
      }
    ]
  },
